==Strategy==
Do whatever it takes to delay Okame and stall out waves of Miz Devils, after which you can slowly chip Okame. With that amount of interference, it's impossible to defeat Okame without getting past all these Miz Devils. Each wave gets progressively stronger, to the point where any and all manner of defenses will crumble in the face of just how many Miz Devils there are. Bring [[Ototo Corps#Breakerblast|Breakerblast]] and [[Battle Items#Sniper the Cat|Sniper the Cat]] to knock Okame back every so often. It is practically impossible to force her off the [[Cat Base]] if she starts hitting it without them, so it's good to keep them handy. Save any expensive nukers you bring for the final wave.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*[[:Category:Wave Attack Cats|Wave Attackers]]/[[Surge Attack|Surge Attackers]]/[[:Category:Explosion Cats|Explosion units]]: [[Crazed Gross Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Macho Legs]], [[Brainwashed Gross Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Brainwashed Sexy Legs Cat]], [[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Jellycat]], [[Talents|Talented]] [[Li'l Fish Cat (Special Cat)|Li'l Island Cat]], [[Hermit Cat (Special Cat)|Grandmaster Cat]], etc. Mainly used to damage groups of Miz Devils at a time while potentially chipping away at Masked Okame as well. Slime is probably the best to use here due to being a throwaway unit that does heavy damage.
*[[Sushi Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Roe Cat]]/[[Rei Ayanami (???) (Super Rare Cat)|Awakened Ayanami]]: Just like in the previous stage, they can stall Okame in place when the Miz Devils are not present.
*Talented [[Matador Cat (Rare Cat)|Bellydance Cat]]: If she successfully Dodges, then she can keep a tough Miz Devil stack and Masked Okame from pushing temporarily while also keeping them away from your attackers.
*[[Stone Cat (Rare Cat)|Boulder Cat]]: Boulder Cat's extreme health can stall Okame and any amount of Miz Devils during its very short lifetime, preventing them from advancing and providing some reprieve to dispatch other units.
*Talented [[Li'l Fish Cat (Special Cat)|Li'l Island Cat]]: With Talents, Li'l Island Cat can Target [[:Category:Aku Enemies|Aku]] in addition to [[:Category:Red Enemies|Red]], which combined with its Wave Attack talent can occasionally shred hordes of Miz Devils.
*[[Cutter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Neo Cutter Cat]]: Can rush in and deal a good amount of damage when no Miz Devils are in the way, useful for chipping Okame in the end.
*[[Crazed Fish Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Island Cat]]: In the same way as in the previous stages, Manic Island Cat can chip Okame slowly once the Miz Devils waves run out.
*[[Brainwashed Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Brainwashed Cat]]: Having a 30% Dodge chance against Dark and Aku, low cost and good speed, Brainwashed Cat is an excellent disposable meatshield that can occasionally hold the line and supplement Boulder when its ability comes into play.
*[[Ancient Egg: N109 (Rare Cat)|Barrel Cat]]: Provided you have them, has a 60% chance to OHKO any stack of Miz Devils and save you in a pinch. Don't count on it too much though.
*Talented [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]]: With Talents, Bahamut can easily rip apart a wave of Miz Devils in one attack, making the battleground much lighter for a bit, and he can even survive a hit from Okame.

