==Trivia==
*Okame's Teahouse's Japanese name, Meido Kissa OKAME (冥土喫茶OKAME), makes a pun: normally ''meido kissa'' would mean "maid café", but the stage's name spells ''meido'' as 冥土, meaning the underworld; the world of the dead. Like [[The Pure Land (Merciless)|The Pure Land]], 冥土 is a Buddhist term.
**The first [[PONOS Corporation|PONOS]] game to use this pun was [[Kyoutou Project]], where the enemy [https://youtu.be/MOXlZjrQPb0 Meido no Oni] (冥土の鬼) was both hellish and dressed as a maid.

